# Store and check out every file byte for byte, on every platform.
#
# Without this, git rewrites line endings in text files on the way in and
# on the way out, so a clone on Linux hands you different bytes than a
# clone on Windows -- and then neither matches the SHA-256 in
# CHECKSUMS.txt. The checksums are the point of this repository, so no
# file here may be translated on its way to you.
* -text
